=== (B) free fall from rest, body-level velocity gate ===
  rddot at rest = GM*v_s**2*(epsilon + 1)/(r*(2*GM*epsilon - r*v_s**2))
  rddot/(-GM/r^2) to first order in eps = 2*GM*epsilon/(r*v_s**2) + epsilon + 1
  Earth pole: v_c^2 = GM_E/R_pole = 62.70 km^2/s^2
   v* =  0.10 km/s: (g_ff/g_N - 1)/eps = 1.254e+04 ; inertia m(1 - 2 eps v_c^2/v*^2) vanishes at eps = 7.97e-05
   v* =  0.17 km/s: (g_ff/g_N - 1)/eps = 4340 ; inertia m(1 - 2 eps v_c^2/v*^2) vanishes at eps = 0.00023
   v* =  0.30 km/s: (g_ff/g_N - 1)/eps = 1394 ; inertia m(1 - 2 eps v_c^2/v*^2) vanishes at eps = 0.000718
   v* =  1.00 km/s: (g_ff/g_N - 1)/eps = 126.4 ; inertia m(1 - 2 eps v_c^2/v*^2) vanishes at eps = 0.00797

=== (C) Born vs classical for the core-making long-range force ===
  Gt/G = 2.37e+31: G m^2/(hbar c) = 3.287e-41; Coulomb (Sommerfeld) parameter Gt m^2/(hbar v) at 30 km/s = 7.79e-06 (Born regime if << 1)
  Gt/G = 3.56e+31: G m^2/(hbar c) = 3.287e-41; Coulomb (Sommerfeld) parameter Gt m^2/(hbar v) at 30 km/s = 1.17e-05 (Born regime if << 1)

=== (D) harmonic core: momentum-only attraction = position attraction (canonical map) ===
  {X_a,P_a} = 1  {X_a,P_b} = 0  {X_a,X_b} = 0  {P_a,P_b} = 0
  H in (X, P): (Omega**2*X_a**2*m**2 + Omega**2*X_b**2*m**2 + P_a**2 + P_b**2 + 2*m*U(Omega*m*(X_a - X_b)))/(2*m)

=== (E) Vainshtein radii for the range of X (u = 1) ===
  lambda_X = 1 kpc: r_V(Sun) = 1189 AU (P18: 1.19e3 AU)
  Earth screens its own surface (r_V = R_E) for lambda_X > 1.21e+11 m
  Sun's r_V encloses 1 AU            for lambda_X > 7.53e+14 m = 0.0244 pc
  Sun's r_V encloses Saturn 9.58 AU  for lambda_X > 2.23e+16 m = 0.723 pc
  Sun's r_V encloses Pluto 39.5 AU   for lambda_X > 1.87e+17 m = 6.06 pc
  two solar-mass stars, lambda_X = 1 kpc: r_V = 1.5e+03 AU (wide binaries beyond this would see G(1 + 4/3) unscreened)

=== (F) gate-width conventions ===
  amplitude gate (notebook, clumping, dark-tests): W = exp(-v^2/(2 v*^2)), v* = sqrt2 mu/m
  rate-form gate used as a potential (program P12-P13, ordinary tests): W = exp(-v^2/v_a^2)
  same width: v_a = sqrt2 v* = 169.7 km/s for v* = 120.0 km/s
